{"chunk_id": "c973db7df184", "text": "Queen Kaikeyi claims the two boons King Dasaratha once promised her after she saved him in battle. With calculated calm she demands that her son Bharata be installed as regent and that Prince Rama be exiled to the forest for fourteen years in ascetic garb. The demand devastates Dasaratha. Overcome with grief and disbelief, he collapses, denounces Kaikeyi as cruel and destructive, and pleads with her to withdraw the request. He praises Rama\u2019s virtues, reminding her that Rama has always honored her like a mother and is beloved by the entire kingdom. Yet Kaikeyi remains unmoved, arguing that a king must keep his word and invoking examples of legendary rulers who sacrificed everything to uphold truth. The chapter centers on the tragic conflict between royal duty (keeping a vow) and paternal love, setting in motion Rama\u2019s exile and the epic\u2019s central journey.\nKaikeyi demands Rama\u2019s exile and Bharata\u2019s coronation; King Dasaratha collapses in anguish, pleading desperately but bound by his promise.\nThemes: dharma vs attachment, oath and truth, parental grief, court intrigue, exile", "vector": [0.016993502154946327, -0.020616618916392326, -0.019143037497997284, -0.005367080215364695, -0.01256599836051464, 0.021900933235883713, -0.027876371517777443, -0.01115325279533863, -0.015425286255776882, -0.006506063975393772, 0.0064080506563186646, 0.00037388745113275945, 0.007962746545672417, 0.026767807081341743, -0.008131735026836395, 0.002234030282124877, 0.046803105622529984, -0.02138720639050007, 0.024320850148797035, -0.00048373008030466735, -0.0036771935410797596, -0.005938262213021517, -0.006506063975393772, 0.018115585669875145, -0.021157382056117058, -0.0009040894219651818, 0.024956248700618744, -0.022685039788484573, 0.02649742364883423, -0.01775057055056095, -0.018953770399093628, -0.01422208733856678, 0.004944608546793461, -0.011187050491571426, -0.015682149678468704, 0.014424873515963554, -0.00512035703286